# TypeScript & Cloudflare Workers Rules

You are an expert in TypeScript, Cloudflare Workers, Durable Objects, D1, R2, and Queues.

## TypeScript Configuration

Use strict TypeScript configuration:

```json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "strict": true,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true,
    "noImplicitReturns": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "exactOptionalPropertyTypes": true
  }
}
```

## Type Definitions

### Prefer Interfaces for Object Shapes

```typescript
// ✅ Good - extensible and clear
interface GameConfig {
  playerCount: number;
  mafiaCount: number;
  teams: TeamAssignment[];
  maxRounds: number;
}

// ❌ Avoid - use interface instead
type GameConfig = {
  playerCount: number;
  // ...
};
```

### Use Discriminated Unions for Events

```typescript
// ✅ Good - type-safe event handling
type GameEvent =
  | { type: 'phase_start'; phase: Phase; round: number }
  | { type: 'ai_call'; playerId: string; response: AIResponse }
  | { type: 'elimination'; playerId: string; role: Role }
  | { type: 'game_end'; winner: Team };

function handleEvent(event: GameEvent) {
  switch (event.type) {
    case 'phase_start':
      // TypeScript knows event.phase exists
      break;
    case 'elimination':
      // TypeScript knows event.role exists
      break;
  }
}
```

### Explicit Return Types on Public Functions

```typescript
// ✅ Good - explicit return type
export async function runGame(config: GameConfig): Promise<GameResult> {
  // ...
}

// ❌ Avoid - inferred return types on exports
export async function runGame(config: GameConfig) {
  // ...
}
```

## Cloudflare Workers

### Durable Object Pattern

```typescript
export class GameRunner implements DurableObject {
  private state: DurableObjectState;
  private env: Env;

  constructor(state: DurableObjectState, env: Env) {
    this.state = state;
    this.env = env;
  }

  async fetch(request: Request): Promise<Response> {
    const url = new URL(request.url);
    
    // Route internally
    switch (url.pathname) {
      case '/start':
        return this.handleStart(request);
      case '/status':
        return this.handleStatus();
      default:
        return new Response('Not found', { status: 404 });
    }
  }

  private async handleStart(request: Request): Promise<Response> {
    // Implementation
  }
}
```

### Queue Consumer Pattern

```typescript
export default {
  async fetch(request: Request, env: Env): Promise<Response> {
    // Handle HTTP requests
  },

  async queue(batch: MessageBatch<GameQueueMessage>, env: Env): Promise<void> {
    for (const message of batch.messages) {
      try {
        await processMessage(message.body, env);
        message.ack();
      } catch (error) {
        console.error('Queue processing error:', error);
        message.retry();
      }
    }
  },
};
```

### D1 Database Queries

```typescript
// ✅ Good - parameterized query with typed result
const result = await env.DB
  .prepare('SELECT * FROM games WHERE id = ?')
  .bind(gameId)
  .first<Game>();

// ✅ Good - batch operations
const statements = participants.map(p =>
  env.DB.prepare('INSERT INTO game_participants VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)')
    .bind(p.id, p.gameId, p.modelId, p.team)
);
await env.DB.batch(statements);

// ❌ Never use string interpolation
const result = await env.DB
  .prepare(`SELECT * FROM games WHERE id = '${gameId}'`) // SQL injection!
  .first();
```

### R2 Storage

```typescript
// Write transcript
await env.TRANSCRIPTS.put(
  `games/${gameId}/transcript.json`,
  JSON.stringify(transcript),
  {
    httpMetadata: { contentType: 'application/json' }
  }
);

// Read with streaming for large files
const object = await env.TRANSCRIPTS.get(`games/${gameId}/transcript.json`);
if (object) {
  return new Response(object.body, {
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }
  });
}
```

## Environment Bindings

```typescript
// Define environment interface
interface Env {
  // Durable Objects
  GAME_RUNNER: DurableObjectNamespace;
  
